<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;ELISIV&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Elisiv is a princess of Kyiv, known for her beauty and intelligence, and later becomes the Queen of Norway through her marriage to Harald III."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HARALD III (HARALD HARDRADA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Harald III, also known as Harald Hardrada, is the King of Norway, a fierce warrior and cunning leader who sought a strategic marriage to strengthen his position."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YAROSLAV THE WISE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yaroslav the Wise is the father of Elisiv and the ruler of Kyiv, known for his political acumen and alliances with European powers."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NORWAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Norway is a country where Harald III ruled and where Elisiv became the Queen after her marriage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KYIV&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kyiv is the capital city of Ukraine, where Elisiv was born and raised in the royal family."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIKING AGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Viking Age is a historical period characterized by the expansion of Scandinavian peoples, including the events surrounding Elisiv and Harald's union."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ICELANDIC SAGAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Icelandic Sagas are medieval texts that chronicle the history of the Viking Age, providing accounts of Elisiv and Harald's marriage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RUSSIAN PRIMARY CHRONICLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Russian Primary Chronicle is a historical text that confirms Elisiv's parentage and her marriage to Harald III."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KAUPANG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kaupang is a Viking Age settlement in southern Norway where artifacts suggest cultural exchange between Norway and Kyiv during the 11th century."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JONATHAN R. R. WALKER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jonathan R. R. Walker is a notable figure in Kyiv's court, known for his quiet confidence and air of authority, and his connection with Elisiv."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PALACE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Palace in Kyiv is the setting for Elisiv's interactions with various nobles and dignitaries, including her encounter with Jonathan R. R. Walker."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROLLING HILLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The rolling hills of Kyiv are the setting for Elisiv's stroll through the palace grounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOBLES AND DIGNITARIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nobles and Dignitaries are the guests at the palace gathering, representing various regions of the realm."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STARS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The stars outside the palace windows are the subject of Elisiv and Jonathan R. R. Walker's conversation."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SILK GOWN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Elisiv's silk gown is mentioned as part of her attire during the palace gathering."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SILVERWARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Silverware is mentioned as part of the dining setup during the palace gathering."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHISPERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Whispers are mentioned as part of the atmosphere in the palace during the gathering."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAVOR OF THE MONARCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The favor of the monarch is a theme in the gathering, with nobles and dignitaries vying for it."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLITICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Politics is a topic of conversation between Elisiv and Jonathan R. R. Walker during their interactions."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LITERATURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Literature is another topic of conversation between Elisiv and Jonathan R. R. Walker during their interactions."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COURT LIFE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Court life is discussed between Elisiv and Jonathan R. R. Walker, highlighting their understanding of the social dynamics."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONNECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A connection is formed between Elisiv and Jonathan R. R. Walker, suggesting a deeper personal relationship."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TAPESTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The metaphor of a tapestry is used to describe the connection between Elisiv and Jonathan R. R. Walker, symbolizing their bond."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fate is personified as bringing people together and weaving their lives into a tapestry of love and loyalty, suggesting a guiding force."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Them refers to two or more individuals whose lives are intertwined by fate, experiencing love and loyalty."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0206</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;ELISIV&quot;" target="&quot;YAROSLAV THE WISE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Elisiv is the daughter of Yaroslav the Wise, who was a powerful ruler and diplomat."</data>
      <data key="d5">"parent-child, royal lineage"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0206</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ELISIV&quot;" target="&quot;HARALD III (HARALD HARDRADA)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Elisiv marries Harald III, becoming the Queen of Norway and strengthening the alliance between Norway and Kyiv."</data>
      <data key="d5">"marriage, political alliance"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0206</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ELISIV&quot;" target="&quot;ICELANDIC SAGAS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Icelandic Sagas provide an account of Elisiv's marriage to Harald III, confirming her status as a historical figure."</data>
      <data key="d5">"historical documentation, confirmation"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0206</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ELISIV&quot;" target="&quot;RUSSIAN PRIMARY CHRONICLE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Russian Primary Chronicle corroborates Elisiv's parentage and her marriage to Harald III, adding historical context."</data>
      <data key="d5">"historical verification, confirmation"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0206</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ELISIV&quot;" target="&quot;JONATHAN R. R. WALKER&quot;">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Elisiv and Jonathan R. R. Walker form a connection based on mutual attraction and shared interests, suggesting a deeper personal relationship."</data>
      <data key="d5">"personal connection, mutual attraction"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0206</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HARALD III (HARALD HARDRADA)&quot;" target="&quot;NORWAY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Harald III rules Norway and seeks to expand his influence through strategic marriages."</data>
      <data key="d5">"leadership, expansion"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0206</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;YAROSLAV THE WISE&quot;" target="&quot;KYIV&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Yaroslav the Wise is the ruler of Kyiv and a key figure in the political landscape of the 11th century."</data>
      <data key="d5">"rule, political influence"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0206</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;NORWAY&quot;" target="&quot;KAUPANG&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Kaupang is a site of cultural exchange between Norway and Kyiv, reflecting the broader historical context of Elisiv and Harald's union."</data>
      <data key="d5">"cultural exchange, historical context"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0206</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FATE&quot;" target="&quot;THEM&quot;">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Fate brings them together and weaves their lives into a tapestry of love and loyalty, indicating a strong guiding influence."</data>
      <data key="d5">"guidance, destiny"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0206</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
</graphml>
